            </div> 
                <p class="snippet" >
                    In <b>Hunter v. Southam</b> Inc., [1984] 2 S.C.R. 145, at pp. 159-60, Dickson J. (as he then was) stated: &nbsp;&nbsp;[...]&nbsp;&nbsp;As this Court stated in <b>Hunter v. Southam</b>, at p. 160, an ex post facto analysis to determine this would be at odds with the purpose of s. 8, which is to prevent unreasonable searches before they occur. &nbsp;&nbsp;[...]&nbsp;&nbsp;[190] <b>Hunter v. Southam</b> (at pp. 159-60) requires that the privacy interests of individuals be balanced against societal interests. 
